<article class="env-lemma" id="0BVA">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0BVA">Lemma <span data-tag="0BVA">48.24.5</span>.</a> If $f : Y \to X$ is a local complete intersection morphism with $X$ a Gorenstein scheme, then $Y$ is Gorenstein. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      By More on Morphisms, Lemma <a href="/tag/07DB" data-tag="07DB">37.62.5</a> it suffices to prove the corresponding statement about ring maps. This is Dualizing Complexes, Lemma <a href="/tag/0DWA" data-tag="0DWA">47.21.8</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>